CORE smt-backend no-new-smt
main.c
--smt2
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
TODO typecast8
^VERIFICATION ERROR$
--
Reading a one-byte struct through a byte-level access used to make the
width==1 fast path of lower_byte_extract emit a typecast(bit-vector ->
struct_tag).  smt2_convt::convert_typecast has no case for a struct/union
destination, so it aborted with the invariant "TODO typecast8 bv ->
struct_tag".  With the fix the byte is converted via bv_to_expr, building
the struct directly, and the (valid) assertion is proved.  Only the SMT2
back-end was affected; the SAT back-end already flattened this correctly.
